 This install applies to "Alone in the Dark", an unofficial Amiga port of
 the Macintosh game by Infogrames and Interplay (1994), original version 1.0.


 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better, an AGA Amiga and a
 68020 or better. A 68030 or faster is recommended. Installation requires
 Installer V43 or later and 8 MB disk space for the game and original data.

 The installed program reserves 2048 KB ChipMem and 6656 KB OtherMem,
 including its Kickstart image. Allow additional memory for the host system,
 WHDLoad and PRELOAD. The tested configuration has 2 MB Chip RAM and 8 MB
 Fast RAM. More Fast RAM allows more of the game data to be cached.

 The game process uses a normal 4 KB stack (about 2.1 KB measured through
 gameplay, Save/Load and exit). Private Macintosh and music stacks are
 allocated internally. No Shell Stack increase is needed.

 The game requires a Kickstart 3.1 image and matching relocation file in
 "Devs:Kickstarts" or "WHDCOMMON:". Supported pairs are:

   kick40063.A600  and kick40063.A600.RTB
   kick40068.A1200 and kick40068.A1200.RTB
   kick40068.A4000 and kick40068.A4000.RTB

 These filenames do not require a particular Amiga model. The relocation
 files are available in the Aminet archive "util/boot/skick346.lha".
 Neither Kickstart images nor original game data are included in this package.


 Installation:
 -------------
 Download the unmodified "AloneInTheDark.img_.sit" StuffIt archive:

 https://www.macintoshrepository.org/download.php?id=5338

 Leave it compressed. Run the Install icon and choose the destination.
 An "Alone in the Dark" drawer is created there.

 If the drawer exists, Keep updates it in place and preserves saved games.
 Remove deletes the whole installation, including saved games. If original
 data is already installed, choose Reinstall or Use existing. The executable,
 overlay, slave, icon and ReadMe are always updated.

 Data installation asks for the archive and a temporary drawer with 24 MB
 free. T: normally uses RAM; choose a hard disk drawer on an 8 MB machine.
 The extractor needs about 2.7 MB of working allocations, plus its code and
 the OS. Extraction may take several minutes. All 74 original-data files
 are verified before replacing installed data; temporary files are removed.

 Start the installed game using its AloneInTheDark icon. PRELOAD is enabled
 by default; disable that Tooltype if there is insufficient memory to cache
 the files. Saved games are kept in the "Saved Games" drawer.


 Features:
 ---------
 - original Macintosh 68k game code and game interfaces
 - complete introduction and game, including the ending and return loop
 - native 320x200 AGA display and hardware mouse pointer
 - Paula music and effects, with music driven by a CIA interrupt
 - original game Save/Load and normal exit to the operating system


 Quitting:
 ---------
 Right-Amiga + Q quits normally and saves pending preferences.
 WHDLoad's QuitKey (F10, changeable with Tooltype "QuitKey=") exits immediately
 without running the game's normal exit code. Save your game before quitting.


 Controls:
 ---------
 Cursor keys         move and turn
 Shift + cursor key  run
 Enter               action/inventory menu
 Escape              back/cancel where supported by the game
 Space + direction   perform the selected action
 S / M               toggle sound effects / music
 Right-Amiga + S     save game
 Right-Amiga + O     load game
 Right-Amiga + Q     quit normally

 If using an emulator, set port 0 to Mouse and port 1 to Nothing. Keyboard
 joystick emulation may otherwise consume the cursor keys.


